Subject: [PATCH] PWA & mobile navigation: resilient cache, legacy-safe
 storage, and shared bottom navigation foundation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

### Motivation

- Provide a Phase‑1 executable foundation of the architecture/PWA refactor focused on PWA stability, storage protection and a shared mobile bottom navigation (女孩｜行程｜班表｜我的｜更多).
- Preserve compatibility with existing inline app modes/URLs, Google Sheets/JSON workflow and local favorites/schedules while avoiding destructive migrations.
- Improve service worker safety so installs/updates cannot silently take over or clear other same‑origin caches and ensure failed network loads do not overwrite the last known good data.

### Description

- Added a configuration-driven navigation system with five mobile destinations and a班表 switcher, implemented in `src/app/navigation-config.js`, `src/app/navigation.js`, and `src/app/navigation.css`, and wired into `index.html` as a module so standalone PWA and mobile web share routing and state.
- Introduced legacy-safe storage helpers in `src/storage/legacy-storage.js` and a resilient data helper `src/services/resilient-cache.js` so malformed localStorage entries are preserved for recovery and failed fetches fall back to last successful data.
- Rewrote the service worker (`sw.js`) to restrict cache cleanup to this project namespace, avoid caching `no-store` requests, make install failures block activation (preventing incomplete takeover), and return explicit offline responses for misses.
- Enhanced `pwa.js` with a user update prompt and controlled `SKIP_WAITING`/`controllerchange` flow, added lightweight build/test tooling (`package.json`, `tools/build-check.js`), unit tests for navigation/storage/sw (`tests/frontend/*.test.js`), and a CI workflow (`.github/workflows/frontend-checks.yml`).

### Testing

- Ran the frontend check suite with `npm run check` (which runs lint/typecheck/tests/build) and the added frontend unit tests completed successfully (`6 passed`) and the static build check passed.
- Executed Node frontend tests directly with `node --test tests/frontend/*.test.js` and they passed; Python backend tests were executed with `python -m pytest -q` and passed.
- Notes on environment limitations: package publishing/PR creation could not be done from this environment because `gh` was unauthenticated and the local MCP `make_pr` tool could not run due to missing runtime/pip access (network/proxy returned 403), and no Chromium binary was available here so automated screenshots / real‑device PWA installation tests were not performed.
- Remaining work: migrate legacy inline features incrementally into modular feature folders, add PNG/maskable icons and physical iOS/Android PWA install verification, broaden E2E coverage and perform real-device update/upgrade tests before recommending merge.
